# Lint and typecheck before finish

Before **`git commit`**, **`st ss` / `st ss --auto`**, or telling the user a branch or PR is ready to merge:

1. Run **`pnpm lint:all`** (same gate as CI: Biome changed-since-staging, Stylelint, **`tsc --strict`**, Knip). Fix failures in the **same turn**; do not push with a red tree.
2. Prefer **`mise run pr-prep`** when opening or refreshing a PR (adds handbook + **`test:changed`**).

Do not run **`pnpm lint:css`** alone and assume the tree is clean — TypeScript and Biome are part of **`lint:all`**.

After CSS edits to `ReleaseSimilarSidebar` or other module CSS, **`lint:all`** is required before commit, not optional.